      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Abnormality of white blood cell number or function has been viewed by some as a relative contraindication to operations done with cardiopulmonary bypass. We have operated upon three patients, each with a different white blood cell abnormality, with good results. We do not believe these patients should be denied operation."},
